# Steps Taken:

* The PDB file of the structure of the human angiotensin-converting enzyme in complex with lisinopril was downloaded from the Protein Data Bank with accession 1O86.
* The .pdf file was then uploaded to PyMOL for structural inspection. Using the ASHLC panel (Action, Show, Hide, Label, Colour), the Cartoon feature, which simplifies the backbone of the protein by showing α-helices as coils and β-sheets as flat arrows,  was isolated. The ligand bonded to it was selected, and the Sticks Feature was used to show active sites.
* This was then saved as a .pse file and the graphical image saved in the .png file format.
* The pdb file of the structure was uploaded to Biovia Discovery Studio for protein cleaning. All chains of the protein were deleted and left with a single chain A. All ligand groups were deleted off the structure. Active sites, water molecules, and other molecules were also deleted from the structure. To ensure a cleaned protein, a single chain A and protein groups were left on the structure.

| Steps                          | Database/Tools Used        | Associated Folder  |
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Retrieval of protein structure | Protein data bank          | Raw_Protein        |
| Inspection of protein          | Pymol                      | Inspected_Protein  |
| Cleaning of protein            | Biovia Discovery Studio    | Cleaned_Protein    |

